/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Generalized\040linear\040mixed\040models\072\040a\040practical\040guide\040for\040ecology\040and\040evolution)
/Author (Benjamin\040M\056\040Bolker\054\040Mollie\040Elizabeth\040Brooks\054\040Connie\040J\056\040Clark\054\040Shane\040W\056\040Geange\054\040John\040R\056\040Poulsen\054\040M\056\040Henry\040H\056\040Stevens\054\040Jada\055Simone\040S\056\040White)
/Subject (How\040should\040ecologists\040and\040evolutionary\040biologists\040analyze\040nonnormal\040data\040that\040involve\040random\040effects\077\040Nonnormal\040data\040such\040as\040counts\040or\040proportions\040often\040defy\040classical\040statistical\040procedures\056\040Generalized\040linear\040mixed\040models\040\050GLMMs\051\040provide\040a\040more\040flexible\040approach\040for\040analyzing\040nonnormal\040data\040when\040random\040effects\040are\040present\056\040The\040explosion\040of\040research\040on\040GLMMs\040in\040the\040last\040decade\040has\040generated\040considerable\040uncertainty\040for\040practitioners\040in\040ecology\040and\040evolution\056\040Despite\040the\040availability\040of\040accurate\040techniques\040for\040estimating\040GLMM\040parameters\040in\040simple\040cases\054\040complex\040GLMMs\040are\040challenging\040to\040fit\040and\040statistical\040inference\040such\040as\040hypothesis\040testing\040remains\040difficult\056\040We\040review\040the\040use\040\050and\040misuse\051\040of\040GLMMs\040in\040ecology\040and\040evolution\054\040discuss\040estimation\040and\040inference\040and\040summarize\040\047best\055practice\047\040data\040analysis\040procedures\040for\040scientists\040facing\040this\040challenge\056)
/Keywords (01\040Mar\0402009\054\040Trends\040in\040Ecology\040and\040Evolution\054\040Generalized\040linear\040mixed\040model\054\040Statistical\040inference\054\040Statistical\040hypothesis\040testing\054\040University\040of\040Florida\054\040Victoria\040University\040of\040Wellington\054\040Miami\040University)
>>
endobj
